| **Does that objection reach the HEADLINE gates? Measured: no.** | The row above is the strongest objection this project has faced, so it was pushed onto gates 1, 4 and 5 rather than left at the corpus where it landed. **Part 1, format:** invalid JSON across both arms is **0 of 158** on gate 1, **0 of 360** on gate 5, and **1 of 158** on gate 4 — on OUR arm. Restricting each gate to documents both arms parsed is therefore a no-op: +46.5 → **+46.5**, +40.4 → **+40.4**, +24.0 → **+24.5**. There are no format failures here for a decoder to fix. **Part 2, schema conformance** (valid JSON is not the same as the right keys): on gate 5 — the only gate whose baseline arm stores predictions — the 30-shot baseline was rebuilt under gold's key paths keeping its own values, which is what a schema-constrained decoder guarantees by construction, and then again forgiving nesting mistakes, which is more than any real decoder gives. **Neither repair moves its score by a single point: 0.5726 → 0.5726 → 0.5726, against an adapted 0.9761. 0.0% of the gap closed.** The cause is measured: across all 360 documents the baseline's key-path precision and recall are both **1.00**, its key set equals gold's on **60/60 documents per tenant**, and it puts the wrong content in **43% of the fields it names correctly**. **So the mechanism on the headline gates is the OPPOSITE of the waybill one — value-level extraction accuracy, which no decoder can supply — and the two together are the scoping result of this project.** Post-hoc analysis of banked data, not a gate, labeled so in the artifact; gold is regenerated from the deterministic generator, never read from a stored copy. The repair function is pinned by a test that fails if it is ever a no-op, because '0.0% closed' is only evidence if the repair demonstrably works | `experiments/schema_conformance_decomposition_2026-08-22.json` | `PYTHONPATH=src python3 scripts/schema_conformance_decomposition.py` |
| **Is the headline an artifact of the corpus's DIFFICULTY? (Addendum H)** | **READING (a): SURVIVES — and it prices the corpus's hardest design choice.** Three seeds per arm, k=10, byte-identical documents across the two mappings, all arms re-run on this host so the comparison is like-for-like. **Control (arbitrary mapping, as the gates run it): baseline 0.5289 → adapted 0.9396, delta +41.07, 56W/0L/4T. Mnemonic mapping (JSON key = the document's own label, which is what real tenant schemas look like): baseline 0.7875 → adapted 0.9750, delta +18.75, 40W/2L/18T, p=2.1e-10.** The mnemonic baseline does **not** saturate (0.7875 < 0.95), so the (u) guard does not fire and the cell is informative. Per the reading frozen before any arm ran: **the effect is NOT an artifact of the arbitrary label→key mapping** — the strongest cheap control anyone proposed against this result, and it survives with the sign test agreeing. **And the honest magnitude, which is the more useful half: the arbitrary mapping is worth +22.3 F1 of the measured delta — more than half of it.** H-B, removing the distractor lines at the arbitrary mapping, costs a further +12.3 (delta +28.79, 46W/2L/12T). The two constants that set this corpus's difficulty account between them for most of the headline. **Read the series and it is coherent rather than convenient:** arbitrary labels + decoys → +41; realistic labels + decoys → +18.8; freight waybills, which have realistic labels and realistic decoys → +9.97 as measured and +4.14 with nothing granted; CORD, real and public → negative. The more the corpus looks like a customer's, the smaller the effect — and H is the first arm to quantify one axis of that instead of inferring it. The design and readings below were preregistered before any arm existed, because an outside technical reader named this as the objection that would end a partner meeting, and they were right. Addendum E varied corpus SHAPE. Nobody had varied corpus DIFFICULTY, which is set by two constants that are hard-coded and never swept anywhere in this repository: the **arbitrary label→key mapping** (the document says `vokrin:`, the JSON calls it `zelbat`, no surface similarity — the generator's own docstring calls this *"the single most important property"*), and **4 distractor lines**. Real tenant schemas do not look like that: a waybill says `Ship Date:` and the key is `ship_date`. And our own evidence is monotone in difficulty, against us: arbitrary-mapping synthetic **+46.5/+24.0/+40.4**; freight waybills with ordinary English labels **+4.14, 5W/5L/17T FAIL**; CORD, real and public, **−7.3/−11.5/−4.5 FAIL**. Design fixed now: `mapping="mnemonic"` makes the JSON key the same token as the document label while the pool is consumed identically, so the two corpora differ in NOTHING else — same documents byte-for-byte, same values, same distractors, same shuffles, pinned by a test. Seeds {1,2,3}, k=10, n_test=20, greedy matched decode, and the arbitrary-mapping control is **re-run on this host** rather than taken from the banked k=10 arms, which ran cuda/bf16. Bar: +5.0 with the sign test agreeing. Readings frozen: **(a)** clears → the effect is not an artifact of the mapping, which is the strongest cheap control anyone has proposed and surviving it is the most valuable thing here; **(b)** positive but under the bar → substantially an artifact, and the headline gets restated everywhere with the mnemonic number beside it at the same size; **(c)** at or below zero → **the headline is an artifact of the generator and these pages will say so in those words**; **(u)** if the mnemonic baseline saturates at ≥0.95 the cell is UNINFORMATIVE, not evidence for (c) — a ceiling cannot show a delta, and that guard is frozen here so a null cannot be banked as a refutation either. **The contingency is frozen too (spec H.6, committed while the first mnemonic cell was still running): saturation is ITSELF a finding against us** — it would mean that on a corpus with realistic labels, plain prompting of a 0.5B model already reaches ceiling from ten examples and there is nothing for adaptation to add, and that goes on these pages in those words regardless of what the follow-up shows — and the only authorised follow-up is the same ablation at **k=4 and k=2** with the bar unchanged, no other amendment | `experiments/novel_schema_h_summary_2026-08-22.json` + 9 cell artifacts | `python3 scripts/addendum_h_summary.py` — the reader was committed while the arms were still running |
