| **Addendum Z — the +46.5 gate, run again with every prediction stored** | **PENDING, RUNNING again since 2026-10-21 20:25Z as restart 3 of seed 1 adapted, no arm banked (three earlier seed-1 adaptations were cut short on 2026-09-23 — two container reboots, one owner compute cutoff; a container rebuild on 2026-10-21 deleted the uncommitted checkpoint folder before anything had been saved; every event is in `experiments/addendum_z_operator_log.jsonl` and the restart counts in `experiments/addendum_z_run_log.json`) — preregistered in `docs/research/ADDENDUM_Z_PROTOCOL.md`, frozen 2026-09-23 and anchored with OpenTimestamps (stamp `2026-09-23T0219Z`) BEFORE the first arm by our own clocks (protocol committed 02:19:23Z, proof 02:19:48Z, first process 02:19:54Z) — the first addendum protocol anchored before its first arm under the `docs/research/ANCHORS.md` policy (the spec's 2026-08-19 and 2026-08-20 anchors also preceded the gates they froze). The proof is complete: the protocol's bytes are attested in Bitcoin block 968216 at 2026-09-23 02:36:37Z, 17 minutes after the first process started, and no document of the run had been decoded by then (the first seed-1 adaptation was still training, and was later killed by a container restart before it saved anything). What the block proves is that the bytes existed before any document of the run was decoded. The run's own start clocks are ours to report; the block time is not (`docs/research/ANCHORS.md`).** The coverage row below says why: the +46.5 headline's six arms banked per-receipt scores and discarded the model outputs, so the step from output to score cannot be re-checked by anyone, and the summary is AGGREGATE. **Design, fixed in the protocol:** the Addendum B gate recipe unchanged — `make_task` seeds {1,2,3}, k=30, eval_n=60, `Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct` on CPU/float32, LoRA r16/α32 for one epoch with the arm seed's demonstration shuffle, the full 30-shot prompt in both arms (B.9.1), vote/rescore 1 greedy + 4 sampled at T=0.7, `max_new_tokens` 512, the 8192-token cap with symmetric exclusion (B.9.2), floor/ceiling on the k-shot arm, and the verdict computed by `scripts/novel_schema_summary.py` **unchanged** under `--date 2026-09-23` — with every pooled completion, each distinct completion's log-probability, the selected text and the raw score stored per document, the adapter's sha256 and weights kept, the environment and thread count recorded, and every process restart counted (sampling is unseeded, as it was: B.9.6). **Readings, by arithmetic:** Z1 the gate word on the new arms (GO / PIVOT / UNINFORMATIVE; UNDECIDABLE withholds); Z2 AGREES if the same word and the gate mean moved ≤ 0.05 from +0.4648, GO BUT MOVED if both GO and it moved more, DISAGREES on a different word; Z3 the largest per-arm absolute difference between the new and the banked mean, published by dated erratum beside B.9.3 as an upper bound on run-to-run spread (run-to-run plus environment, inseparable here) and quoted in place of the single-pair 0.0098 only if larger; Z4 SAME / DIFFERENT EXCLUSIONS on the over-cap documents. **Citation rule, binding whichever way it moves:** the primary-verifiable number replaces +46.5 on every page the day the reading lands, the banked number stays beside it as history, and if Z1 is not GO the headline is withdrawn. **Predictions, written first:** Z1 GO; Z2 AGREES; Z3 ≤ 0.03; Z4 SAME, seed 2 excluding the same 22. **What it cannot show:** a replication by the same operator on a second CPU box is not an independent one — it makes one *possible*. **Cost, from one document decoded before the freeze plus the banked adaptation timings:** ~5–9 minutes per k=30 document at 4 threads and 11.9 GB peak (the protocol's cost paragraph; prose only, not banked), ~2.7–3.2 hours per adaptation on Kaggle (banked arms), ~35–57 wall-hours computed on four cores for the six arms (quoted as 40–60) — the *nine CPU-hours* this page said below was wrong (CORRECTIONS 2026-09-23). The run's launcher, `scripts/run_addendum_z.sh`, changed after the freeze (534e7fd: its liveness check now matches the pid's command line); the recipe code is unchanged, and the run log pins both (`code_pins` in `experiments/addendum_z_run_log.json`). | pending: `experiments/novel_schema_0.5b_k30_seed{1,2,3}_{adapted,kshot}_2026-09-23.json` (the arms, PRIMARY), `experiments/novel_schema_summary_2026-09-23.json`, `experiments/novel_schema_rerun_2026-09-23.json` | `PYTHONPATH=src python3 scripts/novel_schema_rerun.py --run` (resumable, skip-if-exists), then `--read` (withholds until all six arms exist) |
