| **Adaptation-headroom law (Addendum G)** | **UNRUN — no verdict, and the reason is measured.** A post-hoc pattern suggested adaptation's paired advantage falls as the prompted baseline rises. **The full table, including the row this row used to omit:** synthetic baseline 0.43–0.62 → +46.5; waybill hard 0.52 → **+17.5**; waybill **medium 0.72 → +21.1**; waybill mixed 0.94 → +0.0; waybill easy 0.98 → −2.5; CORD, a domain the base model knows → FAIL. **The medium row breaks the pattern** — the baseline rises from 0.52 to 0.72 and the delta rises with it — and this row reproduced the other four while dropping it until 2026-08-22, when an outside auditor found the omission. It is the same defect G.11 was written to name, committed in a second place by the person who wrote G.11. Under G.11's binding rule, the two superseded coupled cells travel with this table too: k=1 delta **+0.0095** at baseline 0.357, k=4 delta **+0.3524** at baseline 0.566 — **both also against the law, on both statistics.** Counting honestly: of the seven data points that exist, three run against the hypothesis. If true it is a buying rule: measure a tenant's prompted baseline first and it predicts whether adaptation is worth anything. It was preregistered in full — bars frozen with zero data in the tree, plus a written commitment to call it a ceiling effect if the headroom-normalised version came out flat — and then **could not be run here**: LOO adaptation costs O(n²) in the pair count, measured at 5.3 s for 1 pair and 1112 s for 4, so the frozen 16-pair design needs ~371 min of adaptation *per arm*, ~100 CPU-hours for the sweep, on a box that recycles every 20–40 min. Deferred to GPU. **Nothing in this repo cites the law as a finding**, and the reader returns UNINFORMATIVE below 10 cells, which is what it returns today. (This row said "nothing in this repo cites the law" while itself reproducing the G.1 table — narrower wording now, because the prohibition is on treating it as evidence, and reproducing the table IS citing it. That is why the table above is now complete.) | none — zero cells banked, by design not by omission; spec G.1–G.10 | `python3 scripts/addendum_g_summary.py` (says so) |
