**Which rows are primary-verifiable, and which are not.** Addendum E/F onward store raw predictions and can be re-scored against gold regenerated from the deterministic generator. **Addendum B — the +46.5 headline — does not**: its arms record per-receipt scores and no predictions, so the step from model output to score cannot be re-checked, only the aggregation of scores already recorded. `verify_from_primary.py` says so rather than passing them silently. The headline is therefore the number on this page with the weakest verification path, and re-running those arms with predictions stored is the fix — priced here until 2026-09-23 as ~9 CPU-hours for the prompted arms, which was wrong (CORRECTIONS 2026-09-23; by the arithmetic of the `ADDENDUM_Z_PROTOCOL.md` cost paragraph, the three prompted arms alone are ~14–24 wall-hours on four cores: 158 scored documents at its 5–9 minutes each, a per-document figure that is prose only, not banked) — preregistered as Addendum Z and not yet landed.
